Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 06:02:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Launch speed: after the 202 a send leaves the intake lane

Misho, 16 Oct: in the tester's 5th 200-seat run a hello took 4 s from the
202 (max 7) against 0.5 s alone. The server's own part, stored to answer,
was 2.3 s median (max 4.5 s). The rest was spent before the run started:
after the 202 the route still wrote the thread status, cleared the goal's
question and stored the owner's message on the intake lane, whose ten
connections every other send in the room was using too - up to 373
queued, ten-second waits ("WITH saved AS (INSERT INTO conversations" 109
slow lines).

Everything after the 202 now runs off the lane, on the ordinary pools.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
